<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Harley-Davidson cut.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Harley-Davidson cut.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Hambrecht &amp; Quist said on Wednesday analyst Shelly Hale Young had cut her rating for motorcycle maker Harley-Davidson Inc to hold from buy.</p>
<p>-- She also trimmed her estimate for 1997 earnings per share (EPS) to $2.19 from $2.25 and set a 1998 EPS estimate of $2.50, a Hambrecht &amp; Quist spokesman said.</p>
<p>-- The analyst downgraded the stock because of weaker-than-expected exports and poor performance in parts and accessories, especially motor clothing. She also believed the shares were fairly valued.</p>
<p>-- Shares in the Milwaukee company were off 2-1/2 to 40-5/8 in heavy mid-morning trade.</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street desk (212) 859-1730))</p>
